translated_text:
REGIONAL GAZETTE

REGIONAL GAZETTE

GUNUNGKIDUL REGENCY

SPECIAL REGION OF YOGYAKARTA

(Official News of the Government of Gunungkidul Regency) Number : 1 Year : 2020

REGIONAL REGULATION OF GUNUNGKIDUL REGENCY NUMBER 1 OF 2020

CONCERNING

THE IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN FROM VIOLENCE

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD THE REGENT OF GUNUNGKIDUL,

Considering : a. that the implementation of protection for women and children victims of violence has been stipulated by Regional Regulation of Gunungkidul Regency Number 25 of 2012;

b. that in accordance with social developments and in order to optimize the protection of women and children victims of violence, Regional Regulation Number 25 of 2012 needs to be amended and adjusted;

c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letters a and b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Implementation of Protection for Women and Children from Violence;

In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 15 of 1950 concerning the Establishment of Regencies within the Special Region of Yogyakarta (State Gazette of 1950 Number 44);

3. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 224, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as amended, most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2015 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);

4. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3143) as most recently amended by Law Number 17 of 2016 (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2016 Number 237, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5946);

5. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);

With Joint Approval of

THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF GUNUNGKIDUL REGENCY

and

THE REGENT OF GUNUNGKIDUL

HAS DECIDED:

To Establish : A REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING THE IMPLEMENTATION OF PROTECTION FOR WOMEN AND CHILDREN FROM VIOLENCE.

text:
Pasal 2

Pelindungan perempuan dan anak bertujuan untuk : a. menjamin terpenuhinya hak-hak perempuan dan anak agar dapat berpartisipasi secara optimal dalam masyarakat sesuai harkat dan martabat kemanusiaan;

b. memberikan pelindungan dan memberikan rasa aman kepada perempuan dan anak dari segala bentuk kekerasan dan diskriminasi;

c. mencegah dan menghapus segala bentuk kekerasan dan ekspolitasi terhadap perempuan dan anak termasuk perdagangan orang;

d. memberikan pelayanan kepada perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan, pelapor, dan saksi; e. memulihkan, menguatkan fisik dan mental perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan; dan

f. meningkatkan kepedulian dan partisipasi masyarakat dalam pencegahan kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak.

translated_text:
Article 2

The protection of women and children aims to: a. ensure the fulfillment of the rights of women and children so they can participate optimally in society in accordance with human dignity;

b. provide protection and a sense of security to women and children from all forms of violence and discrimination;

c. prevent and eliminate all forms of violence and exploitation against women and children including trafficking in persons;

d. provide services to women and children who are victims of violence, reporters, and witnesses; e. restore and strengthen the physical and mental condition of women and children who are victims of violence; and

f. increase awareness and community participation in the prevention of violence against women and children.

text:
Pasal 5

Jenis kekerasan antara lain:

a. kekerasan fisik;
b. kekerasan psikis;
c. kekerasan seksual;
d. penelantaran;
e. eksploitasi; dan/atau
f. kekerasan lainnya.

translated_text:
Article 5

Types of violence include:

a. physical violence;
b. psychological violence;
c. sexual violence;
d. neglect;
e. exploitation; and/or
f. other violence.

text:
Pasal 9

Penelantaran sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 5 huruf d antara lain :

a. perbuatan yang mengakibatkan tidak terpenuhinya kebutuhan anak secara wajar, baik fisik, mental, spiritual maupun sosial yang dilakukan oleh orang tua, wali, atau pihak lain manapun yang bertanggung jawab atas pengasuhannya;
b. perbuatan mengabaikan dengan sengaja untuk memelihara, merawat, atau mengurus anak sebagaimana mestinya yang dilakukan oleh orang tua, wali, atau pihak lain manapun yang bertanggung jawab atas pengasuhannya;
c. perbuatan yang menelantarkan orang dalam lingkup rumah tangganya, padahal menurut hukum yang berlaku baginya atau karena persetujuan atau perjanjian ia wajib memberikan kehidupan, perawatan, atau pemeliharaan kepada orang tersebut; dan/atau
d. perbuatan yang mengakibatkan ketergantungan ekonomi dengan cara membatasi dan/atau melarang untuk bekerja yang layak di dalam atau di luar rumah sehingga korban berada di bawah kendali orang tersebut.

translated_text:
Article 9

Neglect as referred to in Article 5 letter d includes:

a. acts that result in the unfulfillment of a child's needs properly, whether physical, mental, spiritual or social, committed by parents, guardians, or any other party responsible for their care;
b. acts of deliberately neglecting to maintain, care for, or take care of a child as appropriate, committed by parents, guardians, or any other party responsible for their care;
c. acts of abandoning a person within the scope of their household, whereas according to the law applicable to them or due to an agreement or contract they are obliged to provide livelihood, care, or maintenance to that person; and/or
d. acts that result in economic dependence by restricting and/or prohibiting decent work inside or outside the home so that the victim is under the control of that person.

text:
Pasal 10

Eksploitasi sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 5 huruf e adalah :

a. perbuatan yang mengeksploitasi ekonomi atau seksual dengan maksud untuk menguntungkan diri sendiri atau orang lain;
b. perbuatan yang dengan atau tanpa persetujuan korban yang meliputi tetapi tidak terbatas pada pelacuran, kerja atau pelayanan paksa, perbudakan atau praktik serupa, penindasan, pemerasan, pemanfaatan fisik, seksual, organ reproduksi, atau secara melawan hukum memindahkan atau mentransplantasi organ dan/atau jaringan tubuh;
c. memanfaatkan tenaga atau kemampuan seseorang oleh pihak lain untuk mendapatkan keuntungan baik materiil maupun immateriil; dan/atau
d. segala bentuk pemanfaatan organ tubuh seksual atau organ tubuh lain dari korban untuk mendapatkan keuntungan, termasuk tetapi tidak terbatas pada semua kegiatan pelacuran atau pencabulan.

translated_text:
Article 10

Exploitation as referred to in Article 5 letter e is:

a. acts that exploit economically or sexually with the intention of benefiting oneself or others;
b. acts with or without the victim's consent which include but are not limited to prostitution, forced labor or service, slavery or similar practices, oppression, extortion, utilization of physical, sexual, reproductive organs, or unlawfully removing or transplanting organs and/or body tissues;
c. utilizing a person's labor or ability by another party to gain benefits, both material and immaterial; and/or
d. all forms of utilization of sexual organs or other body organs of the victim to gain benefits, including but not limited to all prostitution or indecent acts.

text:
Pasal 12

Pencegahan kekerasan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 3 ayat (2) huruf a dilaksanakan oleh : a. Pemerintah Daerah;

b. keluarga; dan

c. Masyarakat;

d. media masa; dan

e. dunia usaha.

translated_text:
Article 12

Prevention of violence as referred to in Article 3 paragraph (2) letter a is carried out by: a. Regional Government;

b. families; and

c. Community;

d. mass media; and

e. business sector.

text:
Pasal 13

(1) Upaya pencegahan kekerasan yang dilakukan oleh Pemerintah Daerah sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 12 huruf a antara lain :

a. sosialisasi peraturan perundang-undangan yang berkaitan dengan penyelenggaraan pelindungan perempuan dan anak;
b. edukasi tentang bahaya kekerasan dalam rumah tangga;
c. pemetaan wilayah rawan kekerasan;
d. penyusunan data dan informasi tentang perempuan dan anak rawan kekerasan; dan/atau
e. konseling/bimbingan mental dan kerohanian. (2) Upaya pencegahan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dikoordinasikan oleh Dinas.

translated_text:
Article 13

(1) Violence prevention efforts carried out by the Regional Government as referred to in Article 12 letter a include:

a. socialization of laws and regulations related to the implementation of protection of women and children;
b. education about the dangers of domestic violence;
c. mapping of areas prone to violence;
d. compilation of data and information about women and children vulnerable to violence; and/or
e. mental and spiritual counseling/guidance. (2) Prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) are coordinated by the Agency.

text:
Pasal 15

Perempuan dan anak korban tindak kekerasan berhak mendapatkan:

a. Pelindungan;
b. informasi;
c. pelayanan prima;
d. penanganan berkelanjutan sampai tahap rehabilitasi dan reintegrasi sosial;
e. penanganan secara rahasia;
f. pendampingan secara psikologis dan hukum; dan g. jaminan atas hak-hak yang berkaitan dengan status sebagai anggota keluarga maupun anggota masyarakat.

translated_text:
Article 15

Women and children who are victims of violence are entitled to receive:

a. Protection;
b. information;
c. excellent service;
d. continuous handling up to the stage of rehabilitation and social reintegration;
e. confidential handling;
f. psychological and legal assistance; and g. guarantees of rights related to their status as family members and community members.

text:
Pasal 16

Selain mendapatkan hak sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 15, anak korban kekerasan juga mendapatkan hak khusus berupa:

a. hak atas penghormatan dan penggunaan sepenuhnya untuk kelangsungan hidup, tumbuh, dan berkembang;
b. hak pelayanan dasar ;
c. hak pelindungan yang sama;
d. hak bebas dari berbagai stigma; dan
e. hak mendapatkan kebebasan sesuai dengan hukum.

translated_text:
Article 16

In addition to obtaining the rights as referred to in Article 15, child victims of violence also receive special rights in the form of:

a. the right to respect and full use for survival, growth, and development;
b. the right to basic services;
c. the right to equal protection;
d. the right to be free from various stigma; and
e. the right to obtain freedom in accordance with the law.

text:
Pasal 20

(1) Penanganan yang diberikan kepada perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan berupa pelayanan, antara lain :

a. pengaduan;
b. kesehatan;
c. bantuan hukum;
d. Rehabilitasi Sosial;
e. medikolegal;
f. psikologis; dan
g. pendampingan.
(2) Pelayanan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) diselenggarakan dengan:
a. cepat dan tepat;
b. aman dan nyaman;
c. rasa empati;
d. nondiskriminasi;
e. mudah dijangkau;
f. tidak dikenakan biaya; dan
g. dijamin kerahasiaannya

translated_text:
Article 20

(1) Handling provided to women and children victims of violence in the form of services, among others:

a. complaints;
b. health;
c. legal aid;
d. Social Rehabilitation;
e. medicolegal;
f. psychological; and
g. assistance.
(2) Services as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be organized with:
a. prompt and appropriate;
b. safe and comfortable;
c. sense of empathy;
d. non-discrimination;
e. easily accessible;
f. free of charge; and
g. guaranteed confidentiality

text:
Pasal 24

(1) Pelayanan Rehabilitasi Sosial sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 20 ayat (1) huruf d, antara lain:

a. motivasi dan diagnosis psikososial;
b. perawatan dan pengasuhan;
c. pelatihan vokasional dan pembinaan kewirausahaan;
d. bimbingan mental spiritual;
e. bimbingan fisik;
f. bimbingan sosial dan konseling psikososial; g. pelayanan aksesibilitas;
h. bantuan dan asistensi sosial;
i. bimbingan resosialisasi;
j. bimbingan lanjut; dan/atau
k. rujukan.
(2) Bentuk pelatihan vokasional dan pembinaan kewirausahaan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) huruf c, antara lain:
a. pelatihan keterampilan;
b. praktek kerja lapangan;
c. pemagangan;
d. pelatihan keterampilan wirausaha;
e. fasilitasi pembentukan kelompok usaha bersama; f. modal usaha berupa alat penunjang usaha; dan/atau
g. pendampingan pelaksanaan usaha.

translated_text:
Article 24

(1) Social Rehabilitation services as referred to in Article 20 paragraph (1) letter d, among others:

a. motivation and psychosocial diagnosis;
b. care and nurturing;
c. vocational training and entrepreneurship development;
d. mental spiritual guidance;
e. physical guidance;
f. social guidance and psychosocial counseling; g. accessibility services;
h. social assistance and aid;
i. resocialization guidance;
j. advanced guidance; and/or
k. referral.
(2) Forms of vocational training and entrepreneurship development as referred to in paragraph (1) letter c, among others:
a. skills training;
b. field work practice;
c. apprenticeship;
d. entrepreneurial skills training;
e. facilitation of forming joint business groups; f. business capital in the form of business support tools; and/or
g. business implementation assistance.

text:
Pasal 26

(1) Pelayanan psikologis sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 20 ayat (1) huruf f merupakan suatu tindakan yang dilakukan untuk memulihkan psikis perempuan dan anak sebagai korban tindak kekerasan.

(2) Pelayanan psikologis sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) antara lain:

a. melakukan evaluasi psikologis bagi perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan rujukan polisi dengan menggunakan wawancara forensik dengan berbagai teknik;
b. melakukan konseling psikologis individual bagi perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan dengan gangguan psikologis terkait kekerasan yang dialaminya;
c. melaksanakan konseling psikologis keluarga perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan;
d. melakukan psikoterapi individual bagi perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan dengan gangguan psikologis terkait kekerasan yang dialaminya;
e. melakukan psikoterapi kelompok bagi perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan dengan gangguan psikologis terkait kekerasan yang dialaminya;
f. melakukan pendampingan psikologis bagi anak yang berhadapan dengan hukum; dan
g. memberikan keterangan sebagai saksi fakta dalam semua tingkat proses hukum (Berita Acara Pemeriksaan, gelar perkara dan persidangan)
(3) Selain pelayanan psikologis sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1), pelayanan psikologis dapat berupa bimbingan rohani.
(4) Pembimbing rohani sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (3) memberikan pelayanan kepada perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan dalam bentuk pemberian konseling untuk menguatkan dan memberikan rasa aman.

translated_text:
Article 26

(1) Psychological services as referred to in Article 20 paragraph (1) letter f constitute an action taken to restore the psyche of women and children as victims of acts of violence.

(2) Psychological services as referred to in paragraph (1) among others:

a. conducting psychological evaluations for women and children victims of violence referred by police using forensic interviews with various techniques;
b. conducting individual psychological counseling for women and children victims of violence with psychological disorders related to the violence they experienced;
c. implementing family psychological counseling for women and children victims of violence;
d. conducting individual psychotherapy for women and children victims of violence with psychological disorders related to the violence they experienced;
e. conducting group psychotherapy for women and children victims of violence with psychological disorders related to the violence they experienced;
f. providing psychological assistance for children in conflict with the law; and
g. providing testimony as a factual witness in all levels of the legal process (Official Report of Examination, case review and trial)
(3) In addition to psychological services as referred to in paragraph (1), psychological services may be in the form of spiritual guidance.
(4) Spiritual counselors as referred to in paragraph (3) provide services to women and children victims of violence in the form of providing counseling to strengthen and provide a sense of security.

text:
Pasal 27

(1) Pelayanan pendampingan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 20 ayat (1) huruf g dilakukan oleh perorangan atau lembaga yang mempunyai keahlian untuk melakukan konseling, terapi dan advokasi guna penguatan dan pemulihan korban kekerasan.

(2) Pelayanan pendampingan sebagaimana dimaksud ayat (1) meliputi:

a. mendampingi korban selama proses pemeriksaan dan pemulihan kesehatan;
b. mendampingi korban selama proses medikolegal; c. mendampingi korban selama proses mediasi, pemeriksaandi Kepolisian, Kejaksaan dan Pengadilan;
d. memantau kepentingan dan hak-hak korban dalam proses pemeriksaan di Kepolisian, Kejaksaan dan Pengadilan;
e. menjaga privasi dan kerahasian korban dari semua pihak yang tidak berkepentingan, termasuk pemberitaan oleh media massa;
f. melakukan koordinasi dengan pendamping yang lain; dan/atau
g. memberikan penanganan yang bekelanjutan hingga tahap Rehabilitasi Sosial.

translated_text:
Article 27

(1) Assistance services as referred to in Article 20 paragraph (1) letter g are carried out by individuals or institutions that have expertise to conduct counseling, therapy and advocacy for the empowerment and recovery of violence victims.

(2) Assistance services as referred to in paragraph (1) include:

a. accompanying victims during the examination and health recovery process;
b. accompanying victims during the medicolegal process; c. accompanying victims during the mediation process, examination at the Police, Prosecutor's Office and Court;
d. monitoring the interests and rights of victims in the examination process at the Police, Prosecutor's Office and Court;
e. protecting the privacy and confidentiality of victims from all parties who have no interest, including reporting by mass media;
f. coordinating with other assistants; and/or
g. providing continuous handling up to the Social Rehabilitation stage.

text:
Pasal 30

(1) UPT PPA dalam melaksanakan tugasnya sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 29 menyelenggarakan fungsi layanan antara lain: a. pengaduan masyarakat;

b. penjangkauan korban;

c. pengelolaan kasus;

d. penampungan sementara;

e. mediasi; dan/atau

f. pendampingan korban.

(2) UPT PPA memberikan pelayanan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) berpedoman pada standar pelayanan minimal yang telah ditetapkan oleh peraturan perundang-undangan.

translated_text:
Article 30

(1) UPT PPA in carrying out its duties as referred to in Article 29 performs service functions among others: a. public complaints;

b. victim outreach;

c. case management;

d. temporary shelter;

e. mediation; and/or

f. victim assistance.

(2) UPT PPA provides services as referred to in paragraph (1) based on minimum service standards established by laws and regulations.

text:
Pasal 31

(1) Dalam melaksanakan pencegahan kekerasan dan pelayanan kepada perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan, Dinas dapat bekerja sama dengan perangkat daerah/lembaga terkait.

(2) Kerja sama sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilaksanakan dalam bentuk FPKK.

(3) Perangkat daerah/lembaga terkait sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) antara lain perangkat daerah/lembaga yang tugas dan fungsinya di bidang:

a. pendidikan;
b. ketenagakerjaan;
c. kesehatan;
d. sosial;
e. pemberdayaan perempuan dan pelindungan anak;
f. mental dan spiritual;
g. ketenteraman dan ketertiban.
h. kependudukan dan catatan sipil;
i. hukum; dan
j. koperasi dan UMKM.

translated_text:
Article 31

(1) In implementing violence prevention and services to women and children victims of violence, the Service may cooperate with regional apparatus/related institutions.

(2) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented in the form of FPKK.

(3) Regional apparatus/related institutions as referred to in paragraph (1) among others are regional apparatus/institutions whose tasks and functions are in the fields of:

a. education;
b. manpower;
c. health;
d. social affairs;
e. women's empowerment and child protection;
f. mental and spiritual;
g. public tranquility and order.
h. population and civil registration;
i. law; and
j. cooperatives and MSMEs.

text:
Pasal 34

FPKK Kabupaten sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 32 ayat (1) huruf a memiliki tugas antara lain : a. mengoordinasikan dan menyinkronkan upaya penyelenggaraan pelindungan kepada perempuan dan anak dari kekerasan yang dilakukan anggota; b. membangun, memelihara, dan mengembangkan jejaring serta sistem rujukan;

c. mengomunikasikan, menyosialisasikan, dan mengedukasi masyarakat agar berperan aktif dalam pelindungan kepada perempuan dan anak dari kekerasan;

d. melakukan monitoring dan evaluasi;

e. mengoordinasikan pelaksanaan layanan penanganan perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan pada lingkup Kabupaten;

f. menghimpun dan menyebarluaskan data dan informasi yang berkaitan denga penyelenggaraan pelindungan kepada perempuan dan anak dari kekerasan;

g. melakukan pengawasan, pembinaan, dan pendampingan kepada FPKK Kapanewon dan/atau FPKK Kalurahan;

h. menerima rujukan dari FPKK Kapanewon dan/atau FPKK Kalurahan; dan/atau

i. melaporkan pelaksanaan kepada Bupati secara berkala.

translated_text:
Article 34

The Regency FPKK as referred to in Article 32 paragraph (1) letter a has the tasks including: a. coordinating and synchronizing efforts to organize protection for women and children from violence carried out by members; b. building, maintaining, and developing networks and referral systems;

c. communicating, socializing, and educating the community to play an active role in protecting women and children from violence;

d. conducting monitoring and evaluation;

e. coordinating the implementation of services for handling women and children victims of violence at the Regency level;

f. collecting and disseminating data and information related to the organization of protection for women and children from violence;

g. conducting supervision, guidance, and assistance to Kapanewon FPKK and/or Kalurahan FPKK;

h. receiving referrals from Kapanewon FPKK and/or Kalurahan FPKK; and/or

i. reporting implementation to the Regent periodically.

text:
Pasal 36

(1) Instansi Pemerintah sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 35 huruf a paling sedikit meliputi Instansi Pemerintah yang antara lain memiliki tugas dan fungsi di bidang:

a. sosial;
b. penanganan perempuan dan anak;
c. kesehatan;
d. pendidikan;
e. pemuda dan olahraga;
f. agama;
g. kependudukan;
h. ketenagakerjaan; dan/atau
i. perindustrian dan perdagangan.
(2) Lembaga masyarakat sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 35 huruf b dikelompokkan berdasar bidang kegiatannya, antara lain:
a. bidang kesehatan;
b. bidang psikologi;
c. bidang hukum;
d. bidang sosial; dan/atau
e. bidang ekonomi.

translated_text:
Article 36

(1) Government Agencies as referred to in Article 35 letter a at a minimum include Government Agencies that have tasks and functions in the fields of:

a. social affairs;
b. women and children affairs;
c. health;
d. education;
e. youth and sports;
f. religion;
g. population;
h. manpower; and/or
i. industry and trade.
(2) Community institutions as referred to in Article 35 letter b are grouped based on their fields of activity, including:
a. health field;
b. psychology field;
c. legal field;
d. social field; and/or
e. economic field.

text:
Pasal 39

FPKK Kapanewon sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 32 ayat (2) huruf b paling sedikit terdiri dari unsur: a. kesehatan;

b. pendidikan;

c. hukum;

d. psikososial;

e. Masyarakat;

f. kerohanian;

g. forum anak; dan/atau

h. pemberdayaan.

translated_text:
Article 39

The Kapanewon FPKK as referred to in Article 32 paragraph (2) letter b consists of at least the following elements: a. health;

b. education;

c. law;

d. psychosocial;

e. Community;

f. spirituality;

g. children's forum; and/or

h. empowerment.

text:
Pasal 41

FPKK Kalurahan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 32 ayat (2) huruf c paling sedikit terdiri dari unsur: a. kesehatan;

b. pendidikan;

c. hukum;

d. tokoh masyarakat;

e. tokoh agama;

f. forum anak/karang taruna;

g. pamong Kalurahan; dan/atau

h. organisasi/lembaga terkait lainnya.

translated_text:
Article 41

The Kalurahan FPKK as referred to in Article 32 paragraph (2) letter c consists of at least the following elements: a. health;

b. education;

c. law;

d. community leaders;

e. religious leaders;

f. children's forum/youth organization;

g. Kalurahan officials; and/or

h. other related organizations/institutions.

text:
Pasal 43

(1) Masyarakat dapat berperan serta dalam penyelenggaraan pelindungan perempuan dan anak korban tindak kekerasan.

(2) Peran serta masyarakat sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) antara lain:

a. membentuk mitra keluarga di tingkat kalurahan; b. membentuk lembaga masyarakat yang bidang kerjanya di bidang pelindungan perempuan dan anak;
c. melakukan sosialisasi hak perempuan dan anak secara mandiri;
d. melakukan upaya pencegahan jika menemukan indikasi kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak di masyarakat;
e. melakukan pertolongan pertama pada perempuan dan anak korban kekerasan; dan
f. melaporkan kepada instansi yang berwenang apabila di lingkungannya terjadi kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak.
(3) Peran serta masyarakat sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dapat dilakukan oleh perorangan, lembaga masyarakat, lembaga pendidikan, lembaga keagamaan, dan dunia usaha.

translated_text:
Article 43

(1) The community may participate in the organization of protection for women and children victims of violence.

(2) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) includes:

a. forming family partners at the kalurahan level; b. forming community institutions whose field of work is in the protection of women and children;
c. conducting socialization of women's and children's rights independently;
d. conducting prevention efforts if finding indications of violence against women and children in the community;
e. providing first aid to women and children victims of violence; and
f. reporting to the competent authority if violence against women and children occurs in their environment.
(3) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) may be carried out by individuals, community institutions, educational institutions, religious institutions, and the business sector.

text:
Pasal 44

(1) Pemerintah Daerah melibatkan dunia usaha dan pihak swasta untuk berperan serta dalam pelindungan terhadap perempuan dan anak.

(2) Peran serta sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dapat berupa:

a. sosialisasi kepada pegawai di lingkungan usaha mengenai hak-hak perempuan dan anak;
b. sosialisasi kepada pegawai di lingkungan usaha mengenai bahaya tindak kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak;
c. memberikan bantuan dalam penyelenggaraan pelindungan perempuan dan anak sebagai bentuk tanggung jawab sosial perusahaan.

translated_text:
Article 44

(1) The Regional Government shall involve the business sector and private parties to participate in the protection of women and children.

(2) Participation as referred to in paragraph (1) may include:

a. socialization to employees in the business environment regarding the rights of women and children;
b. socialization to employees in the business environment regarding the dangers of violence against women and children;
c. providing assistance in the organization of protection for women and children as a form of corporate social responsibility.
